    "# 2). Palindrome Checker with list:\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "Write a Python function that accepts a string. Inside the function, \n",
    "use a for loop to build a new list containing the characters of the string in reverse order.\n",
    "Then, use an if-else statement to check if the original string is a palindrome \n",
    "(reads the same forwards and backward) by comparing it to the string formed from the reversed list. \n",
    "Print whether the string is a palindrome or not.\n",
    "\n",
    "\"\"\";"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "76c9ccaf-a1e7-4111-b598-e1a85aca0e71",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
